6. Plan Profile Model

After extraction, create one object containing all plan information.

Example:

{

"plan_number":"123456",

"plan_name":"ABC Company 401(k)",

"company_name":"ABC Company",

"company_address":"New York",

"plan_type":"401k",

"plan_year_start":"01/01/2024",

"plan_year_end":"12/31/2024",

"testing_method":"CURRENT",

"top_heavy_percent":62.45,

"top_heavy":true,

"adp_failed":true,

"acp_failed":false,

"returns_required":true,

"fail_402g":false,

"fail_415":true,

"variance_report":true,

"after_12_months":false

}

All business decisions must use this object.

7. File Naming Rule

Final valuation package name:

{PlanNumber}_{BeginningPlanYear}-Valuation.pdf

Examples:

123456_2017-Valuation.pdf

Plan Year:

01/01/2017 - 12/31/2017

→ 2017

 

02/01/2017 - 01/31/2018

→ 2017

 

10/01/2017 - 09/30/2018

→ 2017

Use beginning plan year only.

